=== task: mcq easy
title: Halving a million
prompt: An algorithm throws away half of the remaining items at every step, starting with 1,000,000 items. About how many steps until only 1 item is left?
* About 20 :: Right. 2²⁰ is about a million, so about 20 halvings take a million down to 1.
- About 500,000 :: That's how many items are left after the first step, not the number of steps.
- About 1,000 :: 1,000 × 1,000 is a million, but halving shrinks the items much faster than that.
- About 1,000,000 :: That's one step per item, like linear search. Halving gets there far sooner.
hint: 2¹⁰ is about a thousand.
hint: So 2²⁰ is about a thousand thousands: a million.
right: log₂ 1,000,000 is about 20. Halving is so powerful that even a billion items need only about 30 steps.
wrong: Each step halves the items: a million, 500,000, 250,000, ... After about 20 halvings, 1 is left, because 2²⁰ is about a million.

