title: Halving 90
code:
```python
n = 90
seen = []
while n > 1:
    n = n // 2
    seen.append(n)
print(seen, len(seen))
```
wrong[[45, 23, 12, 6, 3, 2, 1] 7]: `//` rounds **down**: 45 // 2 is 22, not 23.
wrong[[45, 22, 11, 5, 2, 1, 0] 7]: The loop stops when n is 1, because `1 > 1` is False. It never halves 1.
